# Newly added. Line ending rules: tell git which line ending each file type uses when it's checked out on anyone's computer.
# Background: Windows line endings are CRLF (\r\n), Mac/Linux use LF (\n).
#       The container is Linux; if a .sh script turns into CRLF, every line ends with an extra \r,
#       and the container throws errors like "bad interpreter" at startup and won't start at all.

# .sh scripts: always use LF, whether the code is pulled on Windows or Mac
*.sh text eol=lf
